// One refusal names the definition's declared variable two ways: `'a1` in
// the mismatch and `'a` in the note that says what to write.
//
// Run: /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix --no-cache --check \
//        design/review-2026-11-16/repro/t-tvar-b-declared-name-numbered-apart.gx
//
// Expected: the variable the program wrote prints as `'a` throughout, and
//   the callee's copy of its own `'a` (uniq's) is the one numbered apart:
//     type mismatch 'a1: unbound within Discernible does not contain
//     'a: unbound within Any: the body needs 'a within Discernible, ..
// Observed:
//     type mismatch 'a: unbound within Discernible does not contain
//     'a1: unbound within Any: the body needs 'a within Discernible, which
//     the signature does not declare: write 'a: Discernible
//   The `'a` of the first half is uniq's variable, the `'a` of the second
//   half is the program's, and no `'a1` is written anywhere in the program.
let f = 'a: Any |x: 'a| uniq(x);
f(1)
